 ## Background
-The Terminal Rendering Pipeline is an unofficial method described in the GitHub repository [JamesRicher/TerminalSignedDistanceFieldRenderer](https://github.com/JamesRicher/TerminalSignedDistanceFieldRenderer) [S1, unofficial]. It demonstrates how to render 3D scenes using only text-based output, leveraging raymarching and ASCII art techniques. The method is part of a broader trend of "ASCII art" rendering and terminal-based graphics, which have been explored in various contexts for their novelty and low resource requirements [S1, unofficial].
